  <p>
    <strong>Bitcoin and a slew of digital currency markets are seeing significant losses on Sunday as a majority of coins are down between 2-15% during the last 24 hours. The entire crypto-economy has dropped more than 6% and bitcoin dominance is down to 40% the lowest the metric has been in two years. </strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Crypto Markets Face New Lows
  </h2>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      Cryptocurrency markets lost billions on Sunday, as the price of the leading crypto asset bitcoin (BTC) slid from $49,800 to a low of $44,070 per unit. BTC lost 5.5% today and during the past seven days, bitcoin shed more than 20% in value.
    </li>
    <li>
      Bitcoin (BTC) dominance levels have dropped to the lowest levels in two years. Crashing to a low of 40% on Sunday, while ethereum (ETH) captures 18.9%. Besides ETH, coins like BNB, ADA, XRP, DOT, and others have been eating away at BTC’s dominance index.
    </li>
  </ul><figure id="attachment_459590" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-459590" style="width: 2416px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-459590 size-full" title="Crypto Markets Take Deep Losses, Global Trade Volumes Skyrocket, Elon Battles Crypto Twitter" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37.jpg" alt="Crypto Markets Take Deep Losses, Global Trade Volumes Skyrocket, Elon Battles Crypto Twitter" width="2416" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37.jpg 2416w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-1024x558.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-768x418.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-1536x837.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-2048x1116.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-696x379.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-1392x758.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-1068x582.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-771x420.jpg 771w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitfinex_btc_usd-sun_16_may_16_47_37-1920x1046.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2416px) 100vw, 2416px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-459590" class="wp-caption-text">BTC/USD on Sunday at 5:00 p.m. (ET). At press time, bitcoin (BTC) is trading for $44,644 per unit.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      The second-largest crypto asset, in terms of market valuation, ethereum (ETH) is down more than 9% today, but has only lost 11% during the last week. ETH is seeing around $42 billion in reported global trade volume on Sunday.
    </li>
    <li>
      This weekend, a number of proof-of-stake (PoS) crypto assets are doing better than assets that leverage consensus models like proof-of-work. On Sunday afternoon, the PoS token peercoin is the second-largest crypto gainer, gathering 97.5% during the last 24 hours.
    </li>
  </ul><figure id="attachment_459589" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-459589" style="width: 2416px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-459589 size-full" title="Crypto Markets Take Deep Losses, Global Trade Volumes Skyrocket, Elon Battles Crypto Twitter" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29.jpg" alt="Crypto Markets Take Deep Losses, Global Trade Volumes Skyrocket, Elon Battles Crypto Twitter" width="2416" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29.jpg 2416w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-1024x558.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-768x418.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-1536x837.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-2048x1116.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-696x379.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-1392x758.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-1068x582.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-771x420.jpg 771w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_16_may_16_38_29-1920x1046.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2416px) 100vw, 2416px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-459589" class="wp-caption-text">ETH/USD on Sunday at 5:00 p.m. (ET). At press time, ethereum (ETH) is trading for $3,377 per unit.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      On Sunday afternoon, Tesla’s Elon Musk has been awfully talkative when it comes to discussing bitcoin (BTC). Musk made some statements to the podcast host Peter McCormack and said: “Bitcoin is actually highly centralized, with supermajority controlled by handful of big mining (aka hashing) companies.”
    </li>
  </ul>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-459600 size-full" title="Crypto Markets Take Deep Losses, Global Trade Volumes Skyrocket, Elon Battles Crypto Twitter" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk.jpg" alt="Crypto Markets Take Deep Losses, Global Trade Volumes Skyrocket, Elon Battles Crypto Twitter" width="1300" height="500" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk.jpg 1300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk-300x115.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk-1024x394.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk-768x295.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk-696x268.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk-1068x411.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/musk-1092x420.jpg 1092w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1300px) 100vw, 1300px" />
  </p>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      In another Twitter exchange, a Twitter account called “Mr. Whale,” said: “Bitcoiners are going to slap themselves next quarter when they find out Tesla dumped the rest of their Bitcoin holdings. With the amount of hate Elon Musk is getting, I wouldn’t blame him…” Musk responded to this tweet and replied: “Indeed” and even tweeted a screenshot of Mr. Whale’s tweet because some people couldn’t see it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      At the time of writing, on 377 exchanges that tally 9,845 crypto assets, the overall crypto economy is valued at $2.107 trillion. There’s also been about $191 billion in reported global trade volume on Sunday according to market aggregators.
    </li>
    <li>
      The top stablecoins by market capitalization are benefitting from the crypto market downturn as stablecoins such as USDT, USDC, BUSD, and more are seeing heavy demand.
    </li>
  </ul>
  
